diff --git a/README.md b/README.md
index 6be6280..94ea0c3 100644
--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -16,27 +16,15 @@ The package entry registers `or3-external-agent` (pane),
 `/api/connect/environments` response. The pane and launcher dispatch
 `or3:external-agents:open-connections` after selecting the Agents sidebar;
 the sidebar opens its connection settings and removes that listener on unmount.
-All registrations, listeners, and the controller are disposed when the plugin
-is disabled. The host bridge changes open Agent panes into empty chat panes
-before unregistering the Agent pane, so disabled tabs do not show an unknown
-pane. The host bridge registers the package's `coding-workspace` profile with
-the same lifecycle.
+All registrations, listeners, the controller and the coding workspace profile are disposed when the plugin is disabled. The host resets panes when their registered pane app is removed.
 
-Activation requires a host supplied `AgentHostPorts` implementation. The
-required UI, legacy workspace KV, and vault storage methods are defined in
-`client.ts` and `src/client/host-ui.ts`. Missing ports fail activation with a
-clear error. The package transport uses the SDK HTTP and stream clients;
-its host file grant stages attachments only in the selected Intern workspace.
-The host authorizes both transports against saved connection URLs, temporarily
-allowing a new URL while the user verifies it. Redirects and unrelated
-destinations are rejected. A session pane opens with its selected record ID.
-Session-only tokens held by the former built-in plugin are not transferred into
-the installed package's memory vault; those connections need a fresh token.
-Persisted PIN-encrypted tokens remain readable from the existing browser key.
+Version 0.2.0 requires `@or3/plugin-sdk` 2.1 and the `or3-trusted-ui-kit-v1` and `or3-trusted-host-v2` features. The package builds its UI, navigation, profiles, Connect integration and transport from public SDK clients. Connection data uses plugin-scoped workspace storage (`connections`); encrypted credentials use the device-local `vault` secret. Observed sign-out removes device-local plugin secrets, while stale-session startup preserves them.
+
+The host copies legacy connection and encrypted-vault bytes, verifies the destination and only then removes the original. Setup requests saved host origins in one host-owned approval prompt. New host verification also asks for approval; revocation immediately prevents subsequent requests. HTTPS and loopback HTTP are accepted, redirects and unrelated destinations are refused. Staging multipart uploads and SSE use the governed SDK transports; protocol interpretation lives in this package. Session-only tokens from a former installation still require re-entry.
 
 Run `bun run test` and `bun run typecheck` for source checks. Run
 `bun ../or3-chat/packages/plugin-sdk/bin/or3-plugin.mjs validate .`, then
 `build .` and `pack .` for package qualification. The built-host smoke in
 `src/client/built-smoke.test.ts` loads the built module and mounts its sidebar.
 
-This checkout is pinned at package version `0.1.1`. Use `bun install --frozen-lockfile` before qualification. Keep `package.json` and `or3.manifest.json` on the same fresh version for each new artifact; a different archive with changed bytes needs a new version before release. This package is private and is installed through OR3's reviewed package flow, not the creator's build-time provider version map.
+This checkout is pinned at package version `0.2.0`. Use `bun install --frozen-lockfile` before qualification. Keep `package.json` and `or3.manifest.json` on the same fresh version for each new artifact; a different archive with changed bytes needs a new version before release. This package is private and is installed through OR3's reviewed package flow, not the creator's build-time provider version map.
